ries made national news—but not \"normal\" by civilized standards. The book was published by Nation Books.","matchedBy":"infobox_book:high","confidence":"high","attribution":{"label":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Another_Day_in_the_Death_of_America","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"},"infobox":{"title":"Another Day in the Death of America","author":"Gary Younge","publisher":"Nation Books (US); Faber & Faber (UK)","publicationDate":"2016","pages":"267 pp.","isbn":"978-1-56858-975-6 }}","language":"English","subject":"Violence in society, social policy","genre":"Non-fiction"},"publisherEvidenceId":"publisher-evidence-wikipedia-another-day-in-the-death-of-america-a-chronicle-of-ten-short-lives-gary-younge"},"sources":[{"id":"source-award-record-carnegie-nonfiction-ala-carnegie-medals-2017-annual-page","label":"ALA Carnegie Medals 2017 annual page","url":"https://www.ala.org/carnegie-medals/2017-winners","accessedAt":"2026-08-01T20:39:08.468Z","confidence":"official","field":"award","note":"Official awards URL: https://www.ala.org/rusa/awards/carnegie-medals"},{"id":"source-award-record-j-anthony-lukas-book-wikipedia-j-anthony-lukas-book-prize","label":"Wikipedia: J. Anthony Lukas Book Prize","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J._Anthony_Lukas_Book_Prize","accessedAt":"2026-08-01T20:39:08.468Z","confidence":"secondary","field":"award","note":"Official awards URL: https://journalism.columbia.edu/lukas"},{"id":"source-award-record-orwell-combined-book-wikipedia-orwell-prize","label":"Wikipedia: Orwell Prize","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orwell_Prize","accessedAt":"2026-08-01T20:39:08.468Z","confidence":"secondary","field":"award","note":"Official awards URL: https://www.orwellfoundation.com/the-orwell-prizes/previous-winners/ The pre-2019 Book Prize accepted both fiction and nonfiction; this record was reviewed as nonfiction."},{"id":"source-open-library-another-day-in-the-death-of-america-a-ch